  <section id="principles" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Shared rules</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Millimetres everywhere</strong>, radians in code (degrees only where a field says so, such as a gear&apos;s pressure angle or a blend angle).</li>
      <li><strong>Z up</strong>, counter-clockwise outer loops, outward-facing triangles.</li>
      <li><strong>Plain data.</strong> Meshes are typed arrays, B-reps are index tables, sketches are entity lists; everything serialises to JSON and diffs in the project history.</li>
      <li><strong>Errors are explicit.</strong> Invalid input throws a <code>RangeError</code> or a kernel error class (<code>SketchError</code>, <code>BooleanError</code>, <code>BudgetExceeded</code>) with a message the assistant can show; results that would be wrong are never returned.</li>
      <li><strong>Bounded work.</strong> Segment and vertex budgets in the mesh kernel, a time budget in the exact kernel, turn limits in threads, subdivision depth in collision checking.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Every number on these pages was produced by running the kernel with Bun against the source in this repository; re-run the snippets to reproduce them.</p>
  </section>

